.TH NVFURY 1 "January 2026" "nvfury 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nvfury \- NVIDIA Open Kernel Module Forge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvfury
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvfury
is a performance-tuned NVIDIA open driver builder for Linux gaming.
It fetches, patches, and compiles NVIDIA open-gpu-kernel-modules with
gaming-optimized settings, compiler flags, and module parameters.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Build Commands
.TP
.B build
Fetch and build optimized NVIDIA kernel modules.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-version \fIVER\fR
Build a specific driver version (e.g., 590.48.01)
.TP
.B \-\-source \fIPATH\fR
Build from local source directory instead of fetching
.TP
.B \-\-latest
Fetch and build the latest release
.TP
.B \-\-patches \fILIST\fR
Apply patches (comma-separated names or 'default')
.TP
.B \-\-force, \-f
Force rebuild even if source unchanged
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be done without building
.RE
.TP
.B install
Install built modules to the system.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-dkms
Install via DKMS (automatic rebuild on kernel update)
.TP
.B \-\-direct
Install directly (manual rebuild needed on kernel update)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-backup
Skip backup of existing modules
.TP
.B \-\-sign
Sign modules for SecureBoot
.RE
.TP
.B rollback
Restore previous driver from backup.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-backup \fIPATH\fR
Specify backup path to restore from
.RE
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove nvfury-installed NVIDIA drivers.
.RS
.TP
.B status
Show what is installed and would be removed
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run, \-n
Show what would be done without doing it
.TP
.B \-\-all
Also remove cache and config directories
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-dkms
Don't remove DKMS entries
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-config
Don't remove modprobe configuration
.TP
.B \-\-restore
Restore modules from backup after removal
.TP
.B \-\-backup \fIPATH\fR
Specify backup path to restore from
.RE
.SS Tuning Commands
.TP
.B tune \fIPRESET\fR
Apply module parameter preset. Available presets:
.RS
.TP
.B gaming
Low latency, maximum performance (recommended for gaming)
.TP
.B balanced
Balance of performance and efficiency
.TP
.B quiet
Power saving, reduced heat/noise
.TP
.B benchmark
Maximum performance for testing
.TP
.B status
Show current tuning status
.RE
.TP
.B profile \fISUBCMD\fR
Export/import tuning profiles in JSON format.
.RS
.TP
.B list
List available presets
.TP
.B show \fIPRESET\fR
Show preset parameters
.TP
.B export \fIPRESET\fR \fIFILE\fR
Export preset to JSON file
.TP
.B import \fIFILE\fR [\-\-apply]
Import profile from JSON (optionally apply)
.RE
.SS Update Commands
.TP
.B check\-update
Check for available driver updates.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send desktop notification if update available
.TP
.B \-\-force, \-f
Force recheck even if recently checked
.RE
.TP
.B update\-daemon \fISUBCMD\fR
Manage automatic update checking.
.RS
.TP
.B enable
Install systemd timer for automatic checking (every 12 hours)
.TP
.B disable
Remove systemd timer
.TP
.B status
Show timer status and last check
.RE
.SS Hybrid Graphics (PRIME)
.TP
.B prime \fISUBCMD\fR
Manage hybrid graphics for laptops with NVIDIA + Intel/AMD iGPU.
.RS
.TP
.B status
Show current graphics mode
.TP
.B offload \fICOMMAND\fR
Run application on NVIDIA GPU
.TP
.B setup
Configure PRIME with X11/modprobe/udev files
.RE
.SS SecureBoot Signing
.TP
.B sign \fISUBCMD\fR
Manage MOK signing keys for SecureBoot.
.RS
.TP
.B status
Show signing key status
.TP
.B setup
Generate MOK signing key pair
.TP
.B enroll
Enroll MOK certificate (requires reboot)
.TP
.B sign \fIPATH\fR
Sign a kernel module
.RE
.SS Benchmarking
.TP
.B benchmark \fISUBCMD\fR
Performance benchmarking.
.RS
.TP
.B run
Run performance benchmark suite
.TP
.B compare \fIFILE\fR
Compare with a previous benchmark
.TP
.B export \fIFILE\fR
Export results to JSON
.RE
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B config \fISUBCMD\fR
Manage nvfury configuration.
.RS
.TP
.B show
Show current configuration
.TP
.B set \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Set a configuration value
.TP
.B reset
Reset to defaults
.TP
.B path
Show config file path
.RE
.TP
.B preflight
Run pre-build compatibility checks.
.SS Information Commands
.TP
.B status
Show current driver status, kernel version, and configuration.
.TP
.B versions
List available driver versions from NVIDIA GitHub.
.TP
.B gpus
Detect and list all GPUs (multi-GPU support).
.TP
.B recommend
Show recommended patches for detected GPU.
.TP
.B patch list
List available patches with descriptions.
.TP
.B cache status
Show ccache statistics.
.TP
.B build\-cache status
Show cached builds and source hashes.
.SS Other
.TP
.B version, \-v, \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.B help, \-h, \-\-help
Show help message.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nvfury/config.json
User configuration file
.TP
.I ~/.cache/nvfury/nvidia\-open/
Cached NVIDIA source code
.TP
.I ~/.cache/nvfury/build\-meta/
Build cache metadata
.TP
.I /etc/modprobe.d/nvfury.conf
Module parameters configuration
.TP
.I /var/lib/nvfury/backup/
Module backups for rollback
.TP
.I /var/lib/nvfury/mok/
MOK signing keys (SecureBoot)
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Build and install with gaming optimizations
.nf
nvfury build
sudo nvfury install --dkms
sudo nvfury tune gaming
sudo reboot
.fi
.SS Update to latest driver
.nf
nvfury build --latest
sudo nvfury install --dkms
.fi
.SS Run game on NVIDIA GPU (hybrid graphics)
.nf
nvfury prime offload ./game
.fi
.SS Set up SecureBoot signing
.nf
sudo nvfury sign setup
sudo nvfury sign enroll
# Reboot and complete MOK enrollment
sudo nvfury install --sign
.fi
.SS Enable automatic update checking
.nf
nvfury update-daemon enable
.fi
.SS Pin to specific driver version
.nf
nvfury config set pinned_version 590.48.01
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B __NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1
Run OpenGL applications on NVIDIA GPU
.TP
.B __GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia
Force NVIDIA GLX library
.TP
.B VK_ICD_FILENAMES=/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/nvidia_icd.json
Force NVIDIA Vulkan driver
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvidia\-smi (1),
.BR dkms (8),
.BR modprobe (8),
.BR mokutil (1)
